flowchart TB
accTitle: Separate internal actions and caller-managed memory handoffs
accDescr: Memory retrieval and reasoning are separate read-only actions. A caller may use typed retrieval results to construct a bounded reasoning request; the dashed handoff is optional and not an automatic pipeline. A caller may separately request a working-memory update or episode recording from an assessment. Episode verification and semantic review use separate capabilities and evidence but do not enforce a distinct original author and reviewer identity. Procedural validation, activation, and rejection enforce author separation; activation also separates the approver from the validator, and replacement activation retires the predecessor inside the repository operation.

    RET[Memory retrieval<br/>read only] --> RESULTS[Typed retrieval result]
    RESULTS -. optional caller-managed handoff .-> REQ[Construct reasoning request<br/>bounded context + evidence refs]
    REQ --> REASON[Reasoning action<br/>read only]
    REASON --> ASSESS[Structured reasoning assessment]
    ASSESS -. optional caller-managed handoff .-> WM[Working-memory update<br/>separate write action]
    ASSESS -. optional caller-managed handoff .-> EP[Episode recording<br/>starts unverified]
    EP --> EREVIEW[Verify or reject<br/>separate capability + evidence]
    FACT[Semantic proposal<br/>PROPOSED] --> SREVIEW[Approve or reject<br/>separate capability + evidence]
    PROC[Procedure draft] --> VALIDATE[Validate<br/>reviewer differs from author]
    VALIDATE --> ACTIVATE[Activate<br/>approver differs from author and validator]
    PROC --> PREJECT[Reject<br/>reviewer differs from author]
    ACTIVATE --> RETIRE[Repository retires prior active version<br/>during replacement activation]
